cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "FITA — Flexible Image Transfer Alpha"
message: "If you use this software or the FITA convention, please cite it."
type: software
abstract: >-
  FITA is a FITS convention for multi-layer astronomical images in which the
  display channel cannot alter the science. Calibrated flux is held in FLUX_*
  extensions and display transparency in paired ALPHA_* extensions, so
  re-selecting a display range changes only what the eye sees and never the
  measured flux. The convention adds per-layer blend modes, non-destructive
  adjustment layers, stereo depth encoding physical ISM penetration, and IVOA
  ObsCore v1.2 provenance, while remaining a valid FITS multi-extension file
  readable by any FITS reader. Ships with a conformance checker and a labelled
  conformance corpus.
authors:
